myAvi MEANS `an Israeli employee` "Avi" `born` (YMD 1988 3 10) `who is` `male`
myBatya MEANS `a person` "Batya" `born` (YMD 1990 6 20) `who is` `female` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 1990 6 20)) `and` `the work of a person who does not work`
myWidowed MEANS `my marriage:` `widowed` `, traces vanished:` FALSE `, abroad against her will:` FALSE
myNoPension MEANS `A widow's pension fact` WITH `entitled to a pension under section 132(1) to (5) or section 252` IS FALSE
myPension MEANS `A widow's pension fact` WITH `entitled to a pension under section 132(1) to (5) or section 252` IS TRUE
myLongWidowing MEANS `my widowing: married` (YMD 2015 1 1) `, died` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, child` TRUE `, separated` FALSE `, entitled` FALSE `, bore` TRUE `, supplement` FALSE
myAviController MEANS `a person` "Avi" `born` (YMD 1988 3 10) `who is` `male` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 1988 3 10)) `and` (`the work of an employee in Israel, controlling` TRUE `, kibbutz member` FALSE `, entitled to wages` TRUE `, police type` FALSE `, insured earlier` FALSE)
myVisitor MEANS `a person` "V" `born` (YMD 1990 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` (`a person living in Israel under` `a visitor's visa and licence of type B/1, B/2, B/3 or B/4, under regulation 5 of the Entry Regulations`) `and` `the work of an employee in Israel`

-- SC-01, SC-11: an employee resident in Israel, insured under Chapter 11, not a housewife: all nine.
#ASSERT `s 335 — the branches in which contributions are payable, from the facts of` myAvi `, her marriage` myMarried `, her spouse` NOTHING `, her widowhood` NOTHING `, her widow's pension` myNoPension `, on` myDay `, reading` rdNow EQUALS LIST `maternity`, `children`, `work injury`, `accident injury`, `unemployment`, `employees' rights in insolvency proceedings`, `disability`, `long-term care`, `senior citizens and survivors`
-- SC-02: a housewife pays no children and no old-age and survivors/maternity contributions: accident, disability, long-term care.
#ASSERT `s 335 — the branches in which contributions are payable, from the facts of` myBatya `, her marriage` myMarried `, her spouse` (JUST myAvi) `, her widowhood` NOTHING `, her widow's pension` myNoPension `, on` myDay `, reading` rdNow EQUALS LIST `accident injury`, `disability`, `long-term care`
-- SC-04: a non-resident-type employee (B/2 visitor): maternity, work injury, insolvency.
#ASSERT `s 335 — the branches in which contributions are payable, from the facts of` myVisitor `, her marriage` myMarried `, her spouse` NOTHING `, her widowhood` NOTHING `, her widow's pension` myNoPension `, on` myDay `, reading` rdNow EQUALS LIST `maternity`, `work injury`, `employees' rights in insolvency proceedings`
-- SC-07, SC-08: a controlling shareholder in a closely held company: no unemployment, no insolvency contributions.
#ASSERT `s 335 — the branches in which contributions are payable, from the facts of` myAviController `, her marriage` myMarried `, her spouse` NOTHING `, her widowhood` NOTHING `, her widow's pension` myNoPension `, on` myDay `, reading` rdNow EQUALS LIST `maternity`, `children`, `work injury`, `accident injury`, `disability`, `long-term care`, `senior citizens and survivors`
-- SC-03: a widow pensioner pays child contributions but not old-age/survivors or maternity.
#ASSERT `s 335 — the branches in which contributions are payable, from the facts of` myBatya `, her marriage` myWidowed `, her spouse` NOTHING `, her widowhood` (JUST myLongWidowing) `, her widow's pension` myPension `, on` myDay `, reading` rdNow EQUALS LIST `children`, `accident injury`, `disability`, `long-term care`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `I. ss 69, 69A, 71 (CH-25 to CH-41)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

GIVEN parents IS A `The parents of a child, for section 69`
      alone   IS A BOOLEAN
      entitled IS A BOOLEAN
      asked   IS A BOOLEAN
      guardian IS A BOOLEAN
      appointee IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The facts of section 69`
`my section 69 facts: parents` parents `, with the father only` alone `, father entitled` entitled `, asked` asked `, guardian` guardian `, appointee` appointee MEANS
    `The facts of section 69` WITH
        `the parents` IS parents
        `the child is with the father only` IS alone
        `the father is entitled to the allowance` IS entitled
        `the parent paid under section 69(a) asked that the allowance be paid to the other parent` IS asked
        `a guardian was lawfully appointed` IS guardian
        `a person was appointed under section 304(a)` IS appointee
        `the Institute's decision under section 69(d)` IS NOTHING

GIVEN f IS A `The facts of section 69`
      d IS A `A decision of the Institute under section 69(d)`
GIVETH A `The facts of section 69`
f `with my decision` d MEANS
    `The facts of section 69` WITH
        `the parents` IS f's `the parents`
        `the child is with the father only` IS f's `the child is with the father only`
        `the father is entitled to the allowance` IS f's `the father is entitled to the allowance`
        `the parent paid under section 69(a) asked that the allowance be paid to the other parent` IS f's `the parent paid under section 69(a) asked that the allowance be paid to the other parent`
        `a guardian was lawfully appointed` IS f's `a guardian was lawfully appointed`
        `a person was appointed under section 304(a)` IS f's `a person was appointed under section 304(a)`
        `the Institute's decision under section 69(d)` IS JUST d

